---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
// The policy must match what actually runs. BaseLayout loads Google Analytics 4
// (G-M2PTQLF903) and Microsoft Clarity on every production page. The Flutter app
// (bulldozer_app) ships no analytics or crash-reporting SDK; from 1.40 it sends
// anonymous daily counts to usage.azenha.ai (lib/usage.dart, lib/usage_stats.dart;
// store/USAGE-ANALYTICS-PRIVACY-DRAFT.md). If either changes, change this page
// in the same commit.
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="BullDozer privacy: the site counts visits with Google Analytics and Clarity; the apps send anonymous usage counts you can turn off, and Ask AI questions.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
      <span class="kicker">Legal</span>
      <h1>BullDozer — Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="sub">Last updated: 17 November 2026</p>

      <p>BullDozer is a free website and app, published by Azenha AI, that turns
      public statistics into charts, country profiles, maps and a data quiz. There
      are no accounts and no ads, and we never sell or share data for advertising.
      The website measures its visits with Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity;
      the apps send anonymous daily counts with no identifier, which you can switch
      off, and, only if you use Ask AI, the country and question you choose.</p>

      <h2 class="pv-h">The website (azenha.ai/bulldozer)</h2>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Analytics</h3>
        <p>Every page loads two analytics services so we can see which pages are
        read and where they break:</p>
        <ul class="pv-list">
          <li><b>Google Analytics 4</b> records page views, how far you scroll, clicks
          on outbound links and downloads, the page that sent you, your device type,
          browser and screen size, and an approximate location (country and city,
          worked out from your IP address).</li>
          <li><b>Microsoft Clarity</b> records the same kind of usage plus mouse
          movement, taps, clicks and scrolling, and can replay a visit as a
          session recording and show it as heatmaps. We use these to find layout
          and usability problems.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Both set cookies in your browser and send this data to Google and
        Microsoft, who process it under their own policies
        (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google</a>,
        <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="noopener">Microsoft</a>).
        We do not see your name or email, we do not combine this data with anything
        else, and we use it only for traffic statistics and fixing the site.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>How to opt out</h3>
        <p>Turn on your browser’s tracking protection, or use a content blocker
        (uBlock Origin, AdGuard, Brave Shields and similar block both services).
        Google also offers an
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">opt-out add-on</a>
        for Google Analytics. Deleting the site’s cookies resets them. The site
        works the same with all of these.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Stored in your browser</h3>
        <p>Your theme choice and similar settings are kept in your browser’s local
        storage, and the site may cache pages and data files so it works offline.
        These stay on your device.</p></div>

      <h2 class="pv-h">The apps (iPhone, Android, Mac, Windows)</h2>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>No accounts, no tracking</h3>
        <p>The apps do not ask for a name, email, phone number or login, and contain
        no advertising or third-party tracking code. Apart from downloading public
        data files (see Network), what leaves your device is the anonymous usage
        statistics below and a question you choose to ask in Ask AI. If the app opens a page of this website, in your browser or inside the app, the
        website section above applies to that page.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Anonymous usage statistics (version 1.40 and later)</h3>
        <p>The app keeps simple daily tallies of how it is used: which screens you
        open and in what order, which features you use (for example sharing a chart
        or finishing the quiz), which indicators and countries you look at, how
        often you open the app and how long you spend in it. It also counts app
        errors (the type of error and where in the code it happened, never the
        error message or anything on screen), a few device settings (your phone’s language, phone or tablet,
        whether the phone is set to dark or light mode, large text) and, on the first run only, where the app
        was installed from, such as a Google Play campaign or a link we shared.
        Each batch also carries the app version, the system (iPhone, Android, Mac
        or Windows) and the day the app was installed.</p>
        <p>Whenever you open or leave the app, it sends these tallies to our server
        at Cloudflare; they are stored in the EU. They carry no device ID, account
        or advertising ID, and nothing you type is sent. Your IP address is used
        only for a short-lived rate limit against abuse and is not kept. The server only adds
        the tallies to totals, so nothing on it can be traced back to you. We use
        the totals only to improve the app.</p>
        <p>This is on by default. To turn it off, open the menu (the top-right
        button) and switch off Share anonymous usage statistics; this also deletes
        the tallies not yet sent. Versions before 1.40 send nothing.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Stored on your device</h3>
        <p>Your favourites, quiz progress and theme preference are saved on your
        device only. Public datasets are cached so the app works offline. This
        never leaves your device and is removed when you uninstall the app.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Network</h3>
        <p>The app downloads public data files from
        <a href={`${base}/`}>azenha.ai/bulldozer</a>. These are plain file requests
        with no personal information. Opening a source or story link opens it inside
        the app or in your browser, and that page is subject to that site’s own policy.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Notifications</h3>
        <p>Any reminders are scheduled as local notifications on your device. No
        notification data is sent to a server.</p></div>

      <h2 class="pv-h">Both</h2>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Ask AI</h3>
        <p>When you pick a country in Ask AI, or type a question there, the
        country and the question are sent to our server at bot.azenha.ai to
        produce an answer. The server passes them, with that country’s published
        figures, to an AI provider — Anthropic (Claude) or Cloudflare Workers
        AI — only to write the answer, under that provider’s API terms. We do
        not store your questions or the answers. Your IP address is used for a
        per-minute limit on questions and is not kept. Nothing is sent unless you
        open Ask AI and choose a country, and in the app not before you allow
        it: the app asks once, before your first question leaves the phone.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Telegram bot</h3>
        <p>If you press Watch in our Telegram bot, it stores your Telegram chat
        id and the country or figure you chose, so it can message you when they
        change — nothing else about you. Stop watching deletes it.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Children</h3>
        <p>BullDozer is suitable for all ages and asks no one for personal data.
        The website’s analytics described above apply to every visitor.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Changes</h3>
        <p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this
        page with a new date.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Contact</h3>
        <p>Questions, or a request about your data? Email <a href="mailto:agent@azenha.ai">agent@azenha.ai</a>.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .pv-h { font-size: 20px; margin: 30px 0 4px; }
  .pv-list { margin: 6px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; }
  .pv-list li { margin: 0 0 6px; }
</style>
